From: TimoxVasio integration work
Subject: [PATCH] audio: allow channel counts above 255

AI-generated local build assistance for human review only. This is not a
submitted Mixxx contribution.

Mixxx's PortAudio enumerator stores ASIO maxInputChannels/maxOutputChannels in
audio::ChannelCount. With an 8-bit value_t, a valid ASIO count of 256 becomes
the invalid sentinel and SoundManager filters the device out. Widen the count
representation so a 256-channel ASIO device remains valid throughout the
existing device-list path.

This patch targets the Mixxx source tree. It is stored here because this task
is constrained to the asio workspace; it has not been applied to or built into
the installed Mixxx application.

This patch text was generated autonomously by AI and requires human review.

diff --git a/src/audio/types.h b/src/audio/types.h
--- a/src/audio/types.h
+++ b/src/audio/types.h
@@ -40 +40 @@
-    typedef uint8_t value_t;
+    typedef uint16_t value_t;
